---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config.mjs";
---

<Base
  title="Licence"
  description="Drift's licence in plain words: free to use for your own work, source available, Apache 2.0 after two years."
>
  <div class="wrap page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Licence</p>
    <h1>Drift's licence <em>in plain words</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Drift is free to use, including for paid client work. The source code is public. The
      one thing you can't do is use it to build a product that competes with Drift.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use Drift for anything: your own projects, your firm's drawings, client work, teaching.</li>
      <li>Read, change and build the source code, and share your changes.</li>
      <li>Install it on as many computers as you like. There's no fee and no account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you can't do</h2>
    <p>
      Offer Drift, or something made from its code, as a commercial product or service that
      stands in for Drift or does much the same job. For example, you can't sell a CAD
      sketcher built from Drift's code, or host Drift as a paid online service.
    </p>

    <h2>Two years later, it's Apache 2.0</h2>
    <p>
      Two years after each version is released, that version also becomes available under
      the Apache License 2.0, a standard open-source licence with no such limit. So every
      version ends up fully open source.
    </p>

    <h2>Which licence applies to which version</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Versions</th><th>Licence</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>0.1.0-alpha.8 and later</td>
          <td>
            <a href={`${site.repoUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE.md`}>Functional Source License 1.1, ALv2 Future License</a>
            (FSL-1.1-ALv2)
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Up to and including 0.1.0-alpha.7</td>
          <td>MIT or Apache-2.0, your choice. These versions stay available under those terms.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Other people's code</h2>
    <p>
      Drift is built with open-source libraries and fonts. Their licences and copyright
      notices are listed in <a href={`${site.repoUrl}/blob/main/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt`}>THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt</a>,
      and in Drift under <strong>About → Licences…</strong>
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      <p>
        This page is a summary to help you understand the licence. It isn't legal advice, and
        if it ever differs from <a href={`${site.repoUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE.md`}>the licence text</a>, the
        licence text is what counts.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: 56px;
  }
</style>
